    "user_request_original": "Design a 21-layer defect-cavity bandpass filter on fused silica substrate using Ta2O5 (high index) and SiO2 (low index). Layer sequence: Ta2O5/SiO2 alternating for 10 layers, central SiO2 cavity layer, then Ta2O5/SiO2 alternating for 10 layers. Initialize thicknesses from iteration 16 candidate gradient_thickness__01 vector. Apply chirp gradient scaling factor of 0.4 to initial thickness distribution. Constrain per-layer thickness perturbation to ±8 nm maximum change between consecutive optimization rounds. Optimize for maximum transmittance at 1550 nm with suppression in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Normal incidence, unpolarized illumination. Total layer count exactly 21. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
